## Sodium hydroxide (caustic soda)
component-sodium-hydroxide = Sodium hydroxide (caustic soda)
    .genitive = sodium hydroxide
component-sodium-hydroxide-description-novice = White pellets. A very caustic substance — it eats into skin. Dissolving in water, it heats the water strongly.
component-sodium-hydroxide-description-school = The alkali NaOH: in water it splits into Na⁺ and OH⁻ ions. Dissolving gives off a lot of heat (−44.5 kJ/mol) — the solution heats up, sometimes enough to spatter.
component-sodium-hydroxide-safety-school = Dangerous: causes severe burns to skin and eyes. At school only the teacher handles it, with goggles and gloves; the pellets go into the water a little at a time, never water onto the pellets.
component-sodium-hydroxide-model-notes = The enthalpy of solution is for an infinitely dilute solution; in a concentrated one it is smaller.
